WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.920
Mythology and folklore are two things often mentioned in tandem and though in some cases

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.600
They are very similar they aren't the exact same

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.340
So, what is the difference between folklore and mythology

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:24.300
in order for us to differentiate between the two we first have to really understand what makes them so similar at their very core

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.840
both mythology and folklore in basic terms are a form of

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.880
Storytelling perhaps the most ancient forms of narrative we have available to us today

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:40.780
You can consider folklore a subset, or a branch of mythology and even vice versa depending on who you're asking

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:47.360
But more often than not it does feel like folklore is the small fish in the much bigger pond that is mythology

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:54.100
Where the difference between them can really be seen is within the stories themselves and what they attempt to explain to us

00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:01.220
Mythology often derives from what many consider to be sacred texts it aims to tell us about the time before we existed

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.040
How we and everything around us were created

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.600
These stories were often held as the truth and so they became part of many people's religion

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.900
They discussed deities and supernatural figures that they believed to be involved in our creation

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:23.220
At a time when our scientific knowledge was very limited these stories provided explanations to things that, we've only really began to understand

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.680
When these religion has lost their following or when they were absorbed into others they began to be referred to as mythology

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:37.760
so even today is most practice religions in a couple thousand years from now could be seen as not much more than just stories of mythology

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.300
Where folklore differs the most from mythology is in time and scale

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.560
mythology clearly focuses on the beginning of time the explanation of Civilization and culture

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:56.200
Whereas the creatures spirits and deities of folklore almost just exist without this need for a religious or cosmic connection

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:03.640
folktales are told on a much smaller scale and often tend to be exclusive to a specific village in town or city

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.180
They do at times include gods and goddesses in their stories but they often do so

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:14.420
With a specific meaning or moral in mind that doesn't solely refer back to creation or divinity

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.180
the way in which tales of mythology and folklore travelled was naturally quite similar

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:25.660
Because at the time they didn't have things like printing houses and education wasn't as widely available as it is today

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.720
meaning many people just couldn't read or write

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:36.740
A select few poets and writers would eventually document these stories hence why we know so much about certain mythologies on a global scale

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:41.380
Although some folklore was documented in poems and various stories it remained a more

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:47.020
Oral form of storytelling a legend that you might have heard of about a witch or some kind of monster

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:52.300
might be quite different or even remarkably similar to one on the other side of the globe

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:57.880
And it's likely that you'll never know because many of these folktales are passed down through songs and dances

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:02.360
We all have that one story or legend local to our town or city

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:08.280
Japan is quite a good example of a country that has a large amount of mythology and folklore that coexist

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:16.120
It has its two establish religions of Shinto and Buddhism where we get these tales of deities and Kami that attempt to explain japan's creation

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:21.780
But it also has a vast amount of creatures and cryptids that tie into much more local. Folklore

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.860
So to summarise mythology and folklore are quite similar in terms of storytelling

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.460
But the main difference is in intention what they aim to explain

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:40.520
One attempts to explain the universe to us and the other is a much smaller scale of storytelling that focuses on specific areas and individuals

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.180
Hopefully you found that explanation somewhat helpful

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.080
As always I've been your host

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.420
mythology and fiction explained

